1
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:11,963
A repository can look healthy from the outside. A clean README. A passing badge. A promising dependency. Then you inherit it.

2
00:00:12,523 --> 00:00:25,370
Most reviews still run on vibes. A glance at the docs. A hunch about the maintainers. Or a model's opinion with no evidence you can check. For a decision this expensive, that is not good enough.

3
00:00:25,930 --> 00:00:38,921
Retract gives a GitHub repository a health score with verified, cited findings across six pillars: security, code quality, testing, architecture, documentation, and dependencies.

4
00:00:39,481 --> 00:00:48,281
The score is composed from what the analyzers actually measured. A pillar nobody could assess is labelled not measured, never treated as clean.

5
00:00:48,841 --> 00:01:01,569
It clones the repository and runs deterministic tools first. Semgrep, gitleaks, dependency scanning, complexity, duplication, tests, docs, and architecture.

6
00:01:02,129 --> 00:01:12,645
A tree-sitter symbol graph maps every import and call, so structural answers come from the code, never from a model's guess. No embeddings. No vector store.

7
00:01:13,205 --> 00:01:22,801
Every claim is re-checked against the source before it counts. Tool-confirmed findings are verified. Agent-only claims remain hypotheses.

8
00:01:23,361 --> 00:01:34,728
High-severity claims wait for a human signature. The approval is recorded, and dismissals feed calibration. The agent cannot publish a score or approve its own finding.

9
00:01:35,288 --> 00:01:40,273
The result is a dossier, not a dashboard. A score with its per-pillar schedule.

10
00:01:40,833 --> 00:01:47,584
Findings cited to file and line, with the exact excerpt. Open one and the source is right there.

11
00:01:48,144 --> 00:01:55,300
Explore the symbol graph directly: callers, callees, imports, and the path between two symbols.

12
00:01:55,860 --> 00:02:02,070
A remediation plan ordered by points gained and effort, ready to download or hand to the agent.

13
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:09,467
History to see whether the repository is getting better or worse, and a trust panel that says what was measured and what was not.

14
00:02:10,027 --> 00:02:17,385
Ask the eve agent why. It answers from the symbol graph and the tool results, and cites the file and line it actually read.

15
00:02:17,945 --> 00:02:29,685
A typed tool for every graph question. Five specialist subagents for security, code, tests, architecture, and docs. One analysis-scoped session.

16
00:02:30,245 --> 00:02:39,721
Repositories are private to the account that added them. GitHub identity and email are verified. Consequential actions pass through an approval gate.

17
00:02:40,281 --> 00:02:52,401
FastAPI, Postgres, Redis, Celery, and a React workspace. Model spend is metered per account. A benchmark harness keeps precision and recall honest.

18
00:02:52,961 --> 00:02:59,048
Deploy it with Docker, or run it locally. Either way, the same evidence trail comes with it.

19
00:02:59,608 --> 00:03:03,375
Retract. Repository health, computed not vibes.
